== 5. Source ==
cmd/handoff/session.go, cmdRole: for the spare, readBinding (the "already" answer) and
heldAnother both run before bind, which is where lockRoles is taken. So the two checks and
the write they allow are not one step (reviewer-2's #803, point 2). I read this and did not
run the paused case.
cmd/handoff/cmds.go, the "sessions" part of handoff on its own: it goes through the
config's roles, and the spare is not among them, so a blocked spare is never listed (T4).
